# `['a\'b']` is one quoted name; `[ 'x' ]`, with spaces, is a bracket, a string and a bracket.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | project ['a\'b'], x[ 'x' ]
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..31
  PIPELINE@0..30
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    PROJECT_OP@4..30
      IDENT@4..11 "project"
      WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@12..20
        NAME_REF@12..20
          QUOTED_IDENT@12..20 "['a\\'b']"
      COMMA@20..21 ","
      WHITESPACE@21..22 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@22..30
        INDEX_EXPR@22..30
          NAME_REF@22..23
            IDENT@22..23 "x"
          L_BRACK@23..24 "["
          WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
          LITERAL@25..28
            STRING@25..28 "'x'"
          WHITESPACE@28..29 " "
          R_BRACK@29..30 "]"
  WHITESPACE@30..31 "\n"
